      "message": "\u003e \u003e What happens if the `events-broker` plugin is unloaded and then loaded again?\n\u003e \n\u003e `events-broker` is a libModule and cannot be reloaded.\n\nSorry, you\u0027re right.\nI meant an events-broker _implementation_, for example `events-kafka` plugin.\n\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e Wouldn\u0027t this `started` flag remain `true` and prevent the `websession` broker from reconnecting?\n\u003e \n\u003e Yes, and that\u0027s exactly what you wanted to avoid, if I am not mistaken.\n\nNot exactly, I wanted to prevent a _double_ connection to the broker, not the ability to _reconnect_.\n\n\n\u003e The broker api does not have an `unsubscribe`; therefore, reloading or restarting isn\u0027t supported at the moment.\n\nThe broker-api _has_ a `disconnect` [method](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/modules/events-broker/+/refs/heads/master/src/main/java/com/gerritforge/gerrit/eventbroker/BrokerApi.java#55).\n\nThat method is called by the events-kafka lifecycle, disconnecting any subscriber when the plugin is unloaded.\n\nAnd this is where I think we have a problem.\n\n1. We unload events-kafka plugin (this disconnects `websession-broker` without resetting the `start` boolean):\n\n```\nssh -p 29418 admin@localhost gerrit plugin rm events-kafka\n```\n\n2. We re-enable the `events-kafka` plugin:\n\n```\nssh -p 29418 admin@localhost gerrit plugin enable events-kafka\n```\n\nThis now fails because `websession-broker` cannot _reconnect_:\n\n```\nssh -p 29418 admin@localhost gerrit plugin enable events-kafka\ncom.google.gerrit.server.plugins.PluginInstallException: Broker api has already been started\n\tat com.google.gerrit.server.plugins.PluginLoader.runPlugin(PluginLoader.java:544)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.server.plugins.PluginLoader.enablePlugins(PluginLoader.java:306)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.sshd.commands.PluginEnableCommand.doRun(PluginEnableCommand.java:34)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.sshd.commands.PluginAdminSshCommand.run(PluginAdminSshCommand.java:35)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.sshd.SshCommand.lambda$start$0(SshCommand.java:88)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.sshd.BaseCommand$TaskThunk.run(BaseCommand.java:532)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.server.logging.LoggingContextAwareRunnable.run(LoggingContextAwareRunnable.java:126)\n\tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.Executors$RunnableAdapter.call(Executors.java:545)\n\tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.FutureTask.run(FutureTask.java:328)\n\tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor$ScheduledFutureTask.run(ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor.java:309)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.server.git.WorkQueue$Task.run(WorkQueue.java:985)\n\tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1090)\n\tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:614)\n\tat java.base/java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1474)\nCaused by: java.lang.IllegalStateException: Broker api has already been started\n\tat com.google.common.base.Preconditions.checkState(Preconditions.java:513)\n\tat com.gerritforge.gerrit.plugins.websession.broker.WebSessionBrokerApiLoadedListener.onBrokerApiStarted(WebSessionBrokerApiLoadedListener.java:63)\n\tat com.gerritforge.gerrit.eventbroker.BrokerApiPluginListener.onStartPlugin(BrokerApiPluginListener.java:48)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.server.plugins.PluginGuiceEnvironment.onStartPlugin(PluginGuiceEnvironment.java:293)\n\tat com.google.gerrit.server.plugins.PluginLoader.runPlugin(PluginLoader.java:533)\n\t... 13 more\nfatal: plugin failed to enable\n```\n\nShould we not re-set the `start` variable when the broker disconnects?",
